hexagon: run the L2 norm of q and k inside the gated delta net ops

The cost

Each gated delta net layer of Qwen3.5 normalizes each head row of q and of
k before GATED_DELTA_NET with build_gdn_l2_norm: SCALE(RMS_NORM(x, eps / n),
1 / sqrt(n)). On HTP0 that is four f32 passes over q and k in DDR for each
layer. On the phone (Qwen3.5-4B Q8_0, one prefill ubatch of 1024 tokens)
the RMS_NORM ops of q and k take 15.9 ms and the SCALE ops 16.8 ms of the
1044 ms of the ubatch. At one token they are four more small ops for each
layer.

The change

htp-gdn-qknorm.h finds the norm chains of q and k of a GATED_DELTA_NET node:
L2_NORM(x, eps), or SCALE(RMS_NORM(x, e), s) without a bias. The match
needs the same norm for q and for k, an epsilon above zero, no other reader
of a replaced tensor (also in another split), no node between a norm op
and the GATED_DELTA_NET that writes the bytes of the raw rows, and no byte
that the raw rows and the output of the op share. The host then
removes the norm ops and gives the op the raw rows and the four values of
the norm in the kernel params (htp/htp-gdn-params.h, the contract of
htp/gdn-step.h):
    r = s / sqrt(max(a * sum(x^2) + b, c))
    L2_NORM(x, eps)          (a, b, c, s) = (1, 0, eps^2, 1)
    SCALE(RMS_NORM(x, e), s) (a, b, c, s) = (1 / n, e, 0, s)
A batch takes the norm with version 2 of the chunked kernel and with the
sequential kernel. A token takes it in GATED_DELTA_NET and in the fused
state step GDN_STATE_STEP. The unfused ops of a state step that the host
runs in place of the fused op (a slot index that is not valid) keep the
norm ops.

GGML_HEXAGON_GDN_QKNORM=0 keeps the norm ops. The preset value is 1. The
fusion also follows GGML_HEXAGON_OPFUSION, and a batch keeps the norm ops
with GGML_HEXAGON_GDN_CHUNK=1, because version 1 of the chunked kernel has
no norm.

test-backend-ops: the cases of GATED_DELTA_NET get the form of the graph as
an option (qk_form 1), and the state step gets the two forms of the norm.
New cases hold the shapes of Qwen3.5-4B (16 k heads for 32 v heads, 128
values): 1024 tokens, 512 tokens with a fast gate, 100 tokens with 5
snapshot slots (the rollback of the MTP draft), and 20 tokens (the
sequential kernel). The perf list gets the case of 1024 tokens.

The results

The functional runs of version 2 with the norm are in the patch before this
one. The phone stage gdnk of 2026-09-25 (tools/stages/gdnk, HTP0,
Qwen3.5-4B Q8_0) runs one build of the series with four switch settings.
Variant D adds this patch to variant C (the conv DMA and version 2). The
DSP op time of one prefill ubatch of 1024 tokens, the median of 6 graphs:
                     C          D
    RMS_NORM         45.5 ms    30.0 ms
    SCALE            15.9 ms    0
    GATED_DELTA_NET  93.0 ms    98.0 ms
    all ops          1049.6 ms  1025.1 ms
The RMS_NORM ops of D are the other norms of the model. At one token the
RMS_NORM ops take 0.51 ms in place of 0.69 ms, the SCALE ops take 0 in place
of 0.17 ms, and all ops take 92.6 ms in place of 95.3 ms.

llama-bench, the median of the rounds that the runner accepts, with A (the
kernels before the series) for comparison:
                  A        C        D
    pp512 t/s     1014.6   1061.5   1088.6
    pp1024 t/s    963.9    999.3    1014.4
    tg32 t/s      10.69    10.67    10.72
    tg32 at 4096  10.26    10.30    10.34
The KL divergence against the naive x86 base (4 chunks of 512 tokens) is
0.000598 +- 0.000040 for D and 0.000584 +- 0.000040 for A. The decode path
(1 chunk, one token for each batch) gives 0.000559 for D and 0.000557 for
A. test-backend-ops passes the 82 cases of the gated delta net ops.

test-backend-ops perf gives 217 us for the case of one token (32 heads) in
place of 77 us. The perf mode puts the same node 8066 times into one graph,
and the host does the norm match for each copy. Each match reads the whole
graph, thus the host time increases as the square of the node count. This
cause is a calculation from the source code, and not a measurement. A graph
of the app has 24 GATED_DELTA_NET nodes, and tg32 does not become slower.

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 with the patches of patches/series above this one.

